WEBVTT

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.910
"The World Formula Theory.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:21.000
This theory was first proposed by
the great alchemist Paracelsus.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.130
It claims that just beyond
the humankind's world

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:30.340
lies a realm wherein the entire mortal
world has been replaced with formulas."

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.310
"Paracelsus believed that if one could
rewrite the world's constitutive formulas,

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:39.600
it would eliminate all sickness

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.520
and steer humankind toward happiness.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.690
He immersed himself in his work,

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:52.490
and before long, he did an experiment
that meddled with the World Formula.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:58.410
But the experiment led to an
accident known as the Babel incident."

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:06.670
"Babel visited upon humankind
all manner of calamities

00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:10.840
and brought unto this world
things that had never before existed.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.600
Flowers that glowed with their own light,

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.060
minerals with a blue radiance,

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:22.520
and red-eyed humanoids
came to be for the very first time.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:27.440
Each one resulted from having its
original constitutive formula rewritten

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.440
after the World Formula was meddled with.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:35.870
That is why we now have airships
equipped with aerodynamic lift generators,

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:39.290
steam locomotives, street lights,
and other inventions.

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:41.410
They are all powered by astermite,

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:46.710
a mineral created by the rewriting
of the constitutive formula for coal.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.340
Vampires came to be

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:52.420
when Babel caused the constitutive
formula for humans to be rewritten.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.140
They are an entirely new species."

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.180
We are, too, teacher?

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.310
That's right.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:07.520
But I doubt few if any of humanity's
children know the truth of the matter.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.820
But we must never forget.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:14.530
Teacher, you look like you're having fun.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.990
Yes, I am. It's quite fun.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:22.580
And I'm certain it will become
ever more fun as time goes by.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:26.290
And it's all because
you came along with me,

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:31.550
my darling kitten, Mon Chaton.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:43.550
THE 
CASE
 STUDY 
OF 
VANITAS

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:51.320
<i>You're pondering the simple things,</i>
<i>pretty much: human emotions, and love?</i>

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:55.700
<i>I hope one day you'll understand</i>

00:02:55.700 --> 00:03:00.280
<i>Too many wounds have left you</i>
<i>patched together, a miserable sight</i>

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:05.540
<i>That doesn't even know</i>
<i>the definition of "alive"</i>

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:13.050
<i>No need to say,</i>
<i>"Just the two of us" or anything</i>

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:21.640
<i>I've a feeling we can understand</i>
<i>each other, and that's fine for now</i>

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:30.610
<i>I love this world,</i>
<i>and the light only you give me</i>

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:35.490
<i>Makes the world I see</i>
<i>through these fractured eyes </i>

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:40.160
<i>Look gleaming and bright</i>

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.750
<i>There's no such thing as a sure thing</i>

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:49.500
<i>But you can see me, can't you?</i>

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:58.340
<i>When sky and void meet, look back</i>
<i>because the dreams will come later</i>

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:10.850
Isn't this carriage far too large?

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.570
I told you we're going to a ball.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:17.240
You're not planning on going
dressed like that, are you?

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:21.030
Please remove this collar
if you're changing.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.870
I'll go wait with Vanitas.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.370
Domi, are you upset about something?

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:35.250
Was it a bad idea to bring Vanitas along?

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:37.920
I thought he should come along

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:41.970
if we were going to learn
more about curse-bearers.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:45.260
But I failed to see things
from your standpoint.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.600
Forgive me, Domi.

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:53.560
I'm simply worried.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.650
It was my Grandfather's bidding

00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:59.740
that led you to join forces
with the book's bearer.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:05.410
But your personal involvement
with curse-bearers?

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:14.130
I believe you've convinced yourself that
what happened back then was your fault.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:22.340
Domi, you smell so good.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:27.720
You haven't dropped a hint
like that in a long time.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.900
But that won't do.
You must tell me what you want.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:39.690
Well, Noé? Do you want to suck my blood?

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:49.160
Yes, Domi. I want to suck your blood.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:50.830
All right.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:54.170
My blood is all yours...

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.500
...<i>mon chéri</i>.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:40.300
Hmm?

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:43.550
What is it? Are you not feeling well?

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.340
No.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:50.760
Masks... Jesters...

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:54.230
I can't help recalling what I saw.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.270
A flower for you.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:06:59.650
Thank you!

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.320
Mother, look, look!

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.320
Isn't that wonderful, Catherine?

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.700
You're so lucky, sis!

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.950
What do you think you're doing?!

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:15.960
Me? What about your little dalliance
while I was right outside the door?

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.130
Dalliance? What are you talking about?

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.590
Domi is a treasured friend.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:26.010
Don't say things that may be misconstrued.
It only invites trouble for her.

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:30.600
You vampires define friendships
in a strange manner.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:34.480
You speak of that little
exchange we had earlier.

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:39.900
That wasn't the first time Noé sucked
my blood simply because he had a thirst.

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:43.150
An Archiviste is forced
to see a person's memories

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.530
the first time they suck their blood.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:49.910
But Noé frowns on prying into
another's memories without their consent.

00:07:49.910 --> 00:07:51.660
That's why--

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:53.080
Where'd Noé go?

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:56.460
It seems you shouldn't
have removed his collar.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:01.670
No matter. Go on in.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:11.680
Just so you know, you may cry
and scream, but it will all be in vain.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.020
I didn't expect to find automatons here.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:19.600
I'd heard that vampires disliked
human technology for the most part.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:22.730
Domi, who is hosting tonight's--

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:28.400
They wandered off? What trouble they are!

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.620
Uncle has yet to arrive?

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.990
There's been no word from him?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.950
None.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:38.620
I hope nothing bad has happened.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:42.840
Just in case, please inform
Marquis Machina about my uncle.

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:45.670
I will keep looking for her.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:52.930
What are <i>you </i>doing here?!
Don't tell me you followed us?!

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.350
No! I...

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:58.140
Master Lucius, who is this person?

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.560
Lucius?

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.730
He is...

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:03.730
He is a friend of mine!

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:04.400
With me!

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:05.270
Huh?!

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:09.070
There's an important matter
we must speak of! Th-This way!

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:21.420
I-I don't understand. Wh-Why now?

00:09:25.380 --> 00:09:27.420
Answer me, human.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:31.300
Why Noé? What are your intentions?

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.840
I wonder...

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:37.640
I won't stop Noé from
working alongside you.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:42.390
I'll even offer what assistance
I can if he so wishes.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:48.530
But if you're trying to use
his power to your advantage...

00:09:55.450 --> 00:09:59.410
Friends, you say? Don't make me laugh.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:04.670
Men only pay heed to women like you
when it's convenient for them.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:15.510
I do not deny that the
Vampire of the Blue Moon exists.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.350
If Noé believes it,

00:10:17.350 --> 00:10:21.180
I'll proceed with the
assumption that your power

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:23.850
and that of
<i>The Book of Vanitas </i>are real.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:28.770
But I don't understand why you,
a bearer of the blue moon's power,

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:33.200
keep babbling on about saving
the vampires of the crimson moon.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.950
It strains credulity.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:39.700
Vanitas should bear
a deep grudge against us.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:44.750
Can you swear you're not
an assassin sent at his bidding?

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:49.130
Does not the very fact that
you've assumed the name of Vanitas

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:53.470
prove that you worship
the Vampire of the Blue Moon?

00:10:57.140 --> 00:10:58.890
Worship?

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:02.470
The Vampire of the Blue Moon?

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:13.320
I see. You do have a point there.

00:11:13.320 --> 00:11:16.030
All the vampires I've come across thus far

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:21.620
have only thought in terms of whether
or not <i>The Book of Vanitas </i>was real.

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:23.750
Fools, one and all.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:30.290
But now I see. I've been going
about this backward.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:37.430
I should have started by burning
my very existence into your brains.

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:55.900
Hear me now, vampires!

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.780
My name is Vanitas.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:02.450
The Vampire of the Blue Moon
passed on to me his name and his book.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:01.280
What is this?

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:03.830
Is this some sort of show?

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:03.830
Yet I'm but a human!

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:05.870
What the devil is he doing?!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.790
First, I shall prove to you
right here, right now,

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:14.170
that I number among
the Clan of the Blue Moon.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.670
This here...

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:17.930
...proves my claim.

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:20.640
He bears the mark!

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:26.480
I trust that everyone here knows
who it was who made this mark.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:30.150
You must sense by instinct

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:33.940
the sort of power
that was granted unto me.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:38.400
Slay him! Tear him limb from limb!

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.790
Feast your eyes.
This is <i>The Book of Vanitas</i>.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.750
It has the power to corrupt
your true names with ease,

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.960
plunging you into
a despair worse than death.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.720
It is the cursed grimoire.

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:03.050
But I assure you,
there is nothing to fear!

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:06.010
Indeed, you are quite fortunate.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:10.060
For I, Vanitas of the Blue Moon Clan,

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:14.980
shall use <i>The Book of Vanitas</i>
not to slaughter you, but to save you!

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.400
Do you hear me?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:23.780
You need only tremble in your humiliation
while you are saved by my own hand!

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:27.200
Whether you seek this or not,

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:30.120
I <i>will </i>save you vampires!

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.460
That very deed

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:33.420
will be my ultimate act

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:37.300
of vengeance against Vanitas!

00:13:41.970 --> 00:13:45.430
I <i>will </i>save the vampires.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:47.470
Now I see.

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.350
That's why you're so...

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.770
Vanitas.

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:04.070
So there you have it!

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:09.620
If any among you are curse-bearers,
do not hesitate to step forward!

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:17.920
I, Vanitas, doctor and vampire specialist,
shall save you without fail!

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.340
Enough of this!

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:20.210
Just kill him!

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:20.760
Huh?

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:23.470
The Clan of the Blue Moon will save us?!

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:27.180
The Vampire of the Blue Moon
is the root cause of curse bearers!

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.850
Kill that human!

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:30.100
Foul creature!

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:32.310
What does he think he's doing?!

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:33.350
I have no idea.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.900
Why cause an uproar here of all places?!

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.560
I have no idea.

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:45.950
Oh, my, so this is what
all the fuss is about.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:51.160
What brings a mortal man here?

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:55.960
He reeks. I fear my nose shall
fall off from his foul human stench.

00:14:55.960 --> 00:14:58.290
Yikes! Is that my sister, Veronica?!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.090
She said she wasn't coming!

00:15:01.090 --> 00:15:05.260
Let us remove that filth without delay.

00:15:16.150 --> 00:15:17.060
Where is he?!

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.610
The human's gone!

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:27.740
Someone spirited away
that human in the wink of an eye.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:30.080
This just got interesting.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.620
Now, good people!
We shall hunt down the mortal.

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:35.160
Just as our forebears did,

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:40.960
let us find and slay the filthy beast,
for his ilk is the bane of our kind!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:50.010
Wasn't that Jeanne who
just carried off Vanitas?

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.930
Huh? Oh, yes it was.

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:55.480
What would possess her to help him?

00:15:55.480 --> 00:16:01.770
I told her I wished to see
the two of you once more.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:05.900
Might you forgive my discourtesy
the other day, Monsieur Noé?

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.820
That day...

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:14.830
I was not thinking straight.
My temper got the better of me.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:17.830
My immaturity brings me nothing but shame.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.880
Please, Luca. Noé alone will suffice.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:26.920
Let's join the search for Vanitas.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:32.140
Both you and I cannot afford to
have Vanitas die here this day.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:33.760
Okay!

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:39.230
Lucky devils! Those lucky devils!

00:16:39.230 --> 00:16:42.060
That sounds like such fun!

00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:48.530
Imagine that.

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:53.030
To think the day would come when
a woman would sweep me off my feet.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:56.540
Indeed, this is the most unexpected--

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:03.460
I didn't think we would
meet again so soon, Jeanne.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:13.760
Jeanne?

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:17.600
A song?

00:17:17.600 --> 00:17:21.440
What is this cacophony?

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:28.690
Curse-bearers?!

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:37.240
What is this?

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:40.830
Several curse-bearers
here all of a sudden?

00:17:45.340 --> 00:17:49.840
Could the voice of the
curse-bearers be behind this?

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:53.220
This is certainly a pickle.

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:54.470
Sis?!

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:55.970
Catherine?!

00:18:03.440 --> 00:18:05.520
Master Lucius!

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:08.570
Thank goodness, you're unharmed.

00:18:16.280 --> 00:18:20.080
Master Luca.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:23.080
You have the urge to suck blood.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:27.170
Jeanne, are you a curse-bearer?

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:35.180
Who are you fiends?!

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:36.720
Noé!

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:39.100
Please stand back!

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:48.070
I am...

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:51.150
Well, no matter either way.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:59.740
You should suck <i>my </i>blood.

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:01.450
What?

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:10.630
I'm offering you my blood.

00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:15.760
Surely you jest. Who would want
the blood of a human such as you?

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.800
You wish to save the boy, don't you?

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:23.980
There's no time to be choosy.

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:28.270
The sweet scent of blood...

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:32.280
What has gotten into you?

00:19:32.280 --> 00:19:37.610
My fangs may be the death of you.

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.910
Why do this?

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:45.210
I don't know.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:49.960
At the moment, I guess
I don't care what happens.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:52.960
No, wait. Perhaps I'm wrong.

00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:08.810
I'm intrigued.

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:13.900
What would it feel like
if you were to suck my blood?

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:20.530
That's right. When all is said
and done, I have fallen for you.

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:23.700
Now then, Jeanne.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:28.710
N-No, not <i>your </i>blood.

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:31.920
Here you go, Jeanne.

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:45.080
Now I see.

00:21:45.080 --> 00:21:50.830
This isn't... half... bad.

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:52.880
I'll ask you once more.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:56.590
Who are you fiends?

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:59.300
Charlatan.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:08.390
That's right. We are known as Charlatan.

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:17.060
Night of Mocking Masks

00:23:48.610 --> 00:23:52.030
Friends
